      "note": "The copied 78-byte PHP witness compiles successfully into an op_array here; line 276 then executes it, so the `set_error_handler` / `$a = new class{}` / `[&$a->\\xff]` sequence reaches the vulnerable runtime path.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "Zend/zend_builtin_functions.c",
      "function": "set_error_handler",
      "line": 1163,
      "code": "ZVAL_COPY(&EG(user_error_handler), &(fci.function_name));",
      "note": "Registers the PoC's closure as `EG(user_error_handler)` and leaves its mask at `E_ALL`, creating the reentrant userland error-handling state that later frees `$a` during the deprecation warning.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "Zend/zend_object_handlers.c",
      "function": "zend_std_get_property_ptr_ptr",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "After `zend_fetch_property_address()` hands the concrete `zobj` and member name into `zend_std_get_property_ptr_ptr()`, `zend_get_property_offset()` classifies the member as a dynamic-property access, there is no existing dynamic slot, and the class has neither `__get` nor `ZEND_ACC_ALLOW_DYNAMIC_PROPERTIES`. On that witnessed path `zend_std_get_property_ptr_ptr()` emits the deprecation via `zend_deprecated_dynamic_property(zobj->ce, name)` and then continues to use `zobj` without pinning or revalidating it. Because the helper receives only `ce` and does not hold a reference across `zend_error()`, the user error handler can destroy the object before control returns. The fix changes this exact call to pass `zobj`, pins it in the helper, and bails out if the callback destroyed it.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "Zend/zend_object_handlers.c",
      "function": "zend_std_get_property_ptr_ptr",
      "line": 1063,
